E1  p -> q.  terms of order eps^-2, eps^-1 (L = log(q^2/r^2), q = Q(1,0), r = eps(cos phi, sin phi)):
    A = [L*(2*Q - epsilon*cos(phi))/epsilon**2, L*sin(phi)/epsilon]
    B = [2*(L*Q - epsilon*cos(phi))/epsilon**2, 0]
    A - [2 q L/r^2 + L (r - 2 (qhat.r) qhat)/r^2] : [0, 0]
    B - [2 q L/r^2 - 2 (qhat.r) qhat/r^2]         : [0, 0]
    F - [L (r - 2 (qhat.r) qhat)/(2 r^2) + (qhat.r) qhat/r^2] : [0, 0]
    order eps^0 of F: [(L*cos(phi)**2 + 2*sin(phi)**2 - 3/2)/Q, -(L + 1)*sin(2*phi)/(2*Q)]
    angular average of the eps^0 term of F: [(L - 1)/(2*Q), 0]
E2  p -> 0 (r = p).
    A - [2 q L/r^2 + 2 (qhat.r) qhat/r^2]          : [0, 0]
    B - [2 q L/r^2 - L (r - 2 (qhat.r) qhat)/r^2]  : [0, 0]
    F - [L (r - 2 (qhat.r) qhat)/(2 r^2) + (qhat.r) qhat/r^2] : [0, 0]
E3  generic q = (0.7,-0.4): max over 64 angles of |F - F_lead| / log(q^2/r^2)  (F_lead = L (r - 2(qhat.r)qhat)/(2r^2) + (qhat.r)qhat/r^2)
    p = q + r : r = 1e-2, 1e-4, 1e-6, 1e-8 : 1.0336 1.086 1.1104 1.1226  (bounded: the remainder is O(log(1/r)))
    p = r     : r = 1e-2, 1e-4, 1e-6, 1e-8 : 1.0336 1.086 1.1104 1.1226  (bounded: the remainder is O(log(1/r)))
